statement:
Let $X$ be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated scheme [def-pc-scheme, def-weil-pbc-quasi-compact-scheme, def-weil-quasi-separated-morphism]. For every scheme $T$, write $\mathcal A_T=\mathrm{QCoh}(\mathcal O_T)$ for the full category of quasi-coherent structure-sheaf modules [pqf-def-coherent, def-weil-sheaf-of-modules-category], with its abelian structure induced from module sheaves (kernels and cokernels are the ambient ones). Let $I_T:D(\mathcal A_T)\to D_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(\mathcal O_T)$ be the functor induced by termwise inclusion [def-weil-abstract-derived-category, def-pc-derived-category]. For an affine open $U\subseteq X$ with inclusion $j:U\hookrightarrow X$ [def-weil-open-immersion], let $j_*$ be the direct image of module sheaves and $Rj_*:D(\mathcal O_U)\to D(\mathcal O_X)$ its derived direct image, computed by K-injective resolutions [def-pc-ringed-spaces-derived-direct-image, def-pc-derived-direct-image]. Assume, for every affine open $U\subseteq X$:
(a) $j_*$ carries quasi-coherent $\mathcal O_U$-modules to quasi-coherent $\mathcal O_X$-modules, so that it restricts to an additive functor $j_*:\mathcal A_U\to\mathcal A_X$;
(b) this functor has a total right derived functor $\Phi_j:D(\mathcal A_U)\to D(\mathcal A_X)$ with unit $\eta:Q_X\circ j_*\Rightarrow\Phi_j\circ Q_U$, in the sense of the universal property of [def-sfb-right-derived-functor] (no K-injective resolutions in $\mathcal A_U$ are assumed);
(c) there is a natural isomorphism $c:I_X\circ\Phi_j\xrightarrow{\sim}Rj_*\circ I_U$ such that, for every complex $F$ of $\mathcal A_U$, the composite $c_{Q_UF}\circ I_X(\eta_F)$ is the canonical map $Q(j_*F)\to Rj_*(QF)$, namely the localization of $j_*(s):j_*F\to j_*J$ for a K-injective resolution $s:F\to J$ in $\Mod(\mathcal O_U)$ [def-pc-ringed-spaces-derived-direct-image]; here $I_X(Q_X j_*F)$ and $I_U(Q_UF)$ are identified with the localizations of the underlying module complexes by [lem-weil-pbc-exact-functor-derived-factorization].
Then $I_X:D(\mathcal A_X)\to D_{\mathrm{QCoh}}(\mathcal O_X)$ is an equivalence of categories. All derived categories here are unbounded; the hypothesis is about the entire derived functors, not only their degree-zero sheaves.
